stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> TypecheckFirst: register_module(delays_other=true)
    [*] --> TypecheckNext: register_module(delays_other=false)
    [*] --> TypecheckDone: register_module_cached

    TypecheckFirst --> TypecheckWorking: take_priority_work_blocking
    TypecheckNext --> TypecheckWorking: take_priority_work_blocking

    TypecheckWorking --> TypecheckBlocked: block_for_typecheck / block_for_macro_codegen
    TypecheckBlocked --> TypecheckFirst: unblock and still delays others
    TypecheckBlocked --> TypecheckNext: unblock and no known waiters

    TypecheckWorking --> TypecheckDone: notify_typecheck_done

    TypecheckDone --> Complete: inmem_done && object_done
    TypecheckDone --> Complete: object_done (ObjectOnly mode)

    TypecheckFirst --> Failed: notify_module_failed
    TypecheckNext --> Failed: notify_module_failed
    TypecheckWorking --> Failed: notify_module_failed
    TypecheckBlocked --> Failed: dependency failed / notify_module_failed
    TypecheckDone --> Failed: late codegen / load failure

    Failed --> TypecheckFirst: re_register_module / reset and retry
    Complete --> TypecheckFirst: re_register_module
    TypecheckDone --> TypecheckFirst: re_register_module

    note right of TypecheckBlocked
        Architectural risk:
        correctness depends on unblock protocol
        and dependency publication discipline.
    end note

    note right of TypecheckDone
        Ready-state risk:
        payload lives outside scheduler,
        so readers rely on publication
        happening before this transition
        becomes observable.
    end note

    note right of Failed
        Recovery path exists,
        but repeated retries can hide
        ownership / publication design issues.
    end note
